        "id": 1000298
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-02-23T04:35:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think what Bruce is saying is that when we are attached to another Chromebook, Snappy may be overcurrenting the chromebook on the otherside by overshooting the 3A limit.\n\nBy applying the 89% coefficient, there\u0027s no overcurrent.",
      "parentUuid": "7556ecef_408e970a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 11,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 11,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "3501a02d8173f90bed71cfedf7236481e8d3a2b4",
